menu "PlantHub Storage"

config PLANTHUB_HISTORY_RAW_CAP
    int "Raw-tier history ring capacity (samples per plant)"
    default 1344 if IDF_TARGET_ESP32C5
    default 2880
    help
        Number of raw-tier storage_rec_t slots kept per plant, ring-buffer
        style (oldest overwritten first). Each ring file is a fixed-size
        preallocation of this many 22-byte records plus a small header, so
        this directly sizes the "storage" littlefs partition's raw-history
        footprint per plant.

        The ESP32-C5 default is lower because its "storage" partition is
        only 384K (see partitions_c5.csv, which trades storage space for
        bigger OTA app slots and dual-band WiFi headroom). Lower only for a
        custom partition table with even less "storage" space; raising it
        risks exhausting the partition once enough plants are actively
        sampled.

        The C6 has no arm and takes the generic 2880, even though its 16 MB
        layout gives "storage" 8000K (partitions_16m.csv) and could hold
        far more -- one plant's raw ring is only about 63 KB at this cap.
        That headroom is banked on purpose (M6a spec section 5): the
        milestone raises no capacity limit on the strength of available
        space alone. Raise this when something actually needs deeper raw
        history, with the reason recorded.

config PLANTHUB_HISTORY_HOURLY_CAP
    int "Hourly-tier history ring capacity (samples per plant)"
    default 720
    help
        Number of hourly-aggregated storage_rec_t slots kept per plant
        (720 hours = 30 days at one bucket/hour). Same ring-buffer
        semantics and per-plant file as the raw tier, just coarser.

endmenu
